  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "A closed drop is not always a finished drop."
    },
    {
      "t": 4.8,
      "text": "We open a drop, and zep hands us a nonce. It matters at the end."
    },
    {
      "t": 10.8,
      "text": "Stage a fact into it."
    },
    {
      "t": 16.8,
      "text": "Now watch what happens if we just close it."
    },
    {
      "t": 22.8,
      "text": "It closed, but look at the state line, and at the anchor. Not finished."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.8,
      "text": "The nonce is still on disk, and zep will print it again."
    },
    {
      "t": 34.8,
      "text": "So we close it again, passing that nonce along."
    },
    {
      "t": 40.8,
      "text": "Sealed this time, with an anchor."
    },
    {
      "t": 44.8,
      "text": "That is the difference, and it is easy to miss."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches that closing a drop without its nonce leaves a provisional record, and where the nonce can be read back from."
}
